  "candidate": "1. Requirements: list goals for customers, stores, riders, admins; cover profiles, addresses, orders, edit/cancel, dispatch/reassign, failed delivery, returns, fees, collections/payouts, support.\n2. Roles: map every action to allowed roles; state owner-only, role-only, admin-only; deny by default; define read/write/delete boundaries.\n3. Data: define entities, ownership, status, timestamps, versions, audit logs; preserve existing data; avoid destructive changes.\n4. States: define order/job statuses and legal transitions; block invalid transitions; keep failed parcels assigned until resolved.\n5. Concurrency: use version checks for edits; use idempotency keys for duplicate submissions; prevent double dispatch, double payout, duplicate orders.\n6. Recovery: specify retry, timeout, reassignment, manual override, compensation for failed delivery/returns; no automatic replay without guard; record collections/payouts only for verified delivered events.\n7. Verification: test happy paths, permission denials, concurrent edits, duplicate requests, failed delivery, returns, fee calculation, payout rules, audit trail, data preservation, rollback/recovery.",
